    "body": "> I think this is normative? Not sure, but I'd lean that way.\r\n\r\nChanged it to normative because yeah agreed that makes more sense. (It’s true that HTML isn’t relying on it for normative requirements for any conformance classes defined in HTML, and that RFC states only one “must” in the entire document, and is “Category: Informational“—but I think those are actually deficiencies in the RFC, since it really does define requirements that search engines implement interoperably.",
